  "task": {
    "objective": "Deliver both physical cargo objects from the east loading bay to the northern goal, using two cross-wired remote gate operators and brief binary broadcasts.",
    "natural_termination": "All two cargo objects delivered ends naturally. Each delivery gives every role +0.5 and the final delivery adds +0.5. Otherwise truncate at step 128. Deliveries redraw both private sensor bits and close both gates.",
    "interaction": "Sensor 0's bit is required at role 1's panel; sensor 1's bit is required at role 0's panel. Only local owners can directly read a sensor. A correct remote pulse opens the corresponding courier gate for six steps; a wrong pulse closes it and jams its operator. Binary messages change what other roles observe for four frames.",
    "observation_access": "Map, role positions, panel attempts, cargo, gate timers, pulse energy, cooldowns and live broadcasts are public. Sensor values are masked to -1 unless the querying role is that sensor's owner and within Manhattan distance one. Role 2 never directly observes either bit. The sensor entity visibility uses exactly the same stored code_visible mask. Expired signal entities are inactive and their observation values are -1."
  },
